      "id": "v1/5nn4_SC2_A_1017__top1/r02/synthesis",
      "evidence_sha256": "b2078de8fce144d7f208755fc16d88aad7d21d81a156581fe6e0bfb582cbd89f",
      "assessment": "R2 synthesis successfully constructs two same-parent contrasts: [7,6,5,5] versus [6,6,5,5], and [4,5,6,5] versus [6,5,6,5]. However it promotes the analysts' false sign conflict and arbitrary 0.03 threshold into shared memory, and marks the tick scale supported as inert before observing the designed contrasts. R3 gives the first pair a +0.027872 mean gap and the second a +0.052994 gap, both concentrated in rare changes.",
      "decision_update": "Retain portfolio-level identifiability as a useful strategy, but compute effect direction from the supplied cross-group evidence and separate observed magnitudes, concentration and inference. Publish unsupported mechanisms as unresolved alternatives. Compare the selected portfolio's information value and expected Mean contribution without hard-coding a universal significance threshold.",
      "counterexample_or_limitation": "The opposite-direction pair does distinguish outcomes on these shared starts, contrary to a blanket inertness claim, but the near-zero medians prevent a broad-benefit conclusion. All sources share original starts; the four arms are paired conditions, not independent replications.",
