      "assessment": "R3 G1 correctly recognizes selected incumbent Mean 4.21307 as a search artifact and latest 4.18890 as lower, while its planning preamble again calls the 0.02417 deficit a positive shift. It compares step-90 current geometry 0.7633 A to step-100 endpoint geometry 0.8183 A as evidence about schedule improvement and says terminal updates are the most numerous, although that interval has 15 updates. H2 [7,6,6,5] is selected and gives R4 Mean 4.188928.",
      "decision_update": "For geometry-based causal arguments, compare like state/head/time quantities under comparable conditions; within-trajectory release drift is a separate question. Derive update counts and integrated effect from metadata. A late-window test can be retained as a limited diagnostic, but remove unsupported quantitative future-score ranges.",
      "counterexample_or_limitation": "The selected H2 mean changes only about +0.000027 from its source result, which supports a very small local response in this run but does not prove the entire window inert. Parent selection and the different state types limit attribution.",
