    {
      "id": "v1/5nn4_SC2_A_1017__top1/r03/G2",
      "evidence_sha256": "9164453c80a313420ea2ee0ed42afd219cd8694e6e74e9ce8e9ce382309c925c",
      "assessment": "R3 G2 uses only automatic history and paired evidence, without any new tool call, and correctly diagnoses the 0.052045 incumbent advantage. It offers [7,5,5,5] and [6,5,6,5] as reallocations but grounds mechanistic claims largely in prior public memory, including its inaccurate inertness framing. H1 is selected and reproduces the prior 4.189977 Mean in R4; H2 is not selected.",
      "decision_update": "Use earlier memory as a retrieval cue rather than verified evidence. When choosing a reallocation because of control strength or drift, consult current interval evidence or explicitly mark those mechanics unmeasured. A repeat should be justified by changed parent/exposure and expected information, not called an independent reproducibility trial by default.",
      "counterexample_or_limitation": "An identical mean under shared RNG and replay is consistent with deterministic path reuse; it is not independent evidence of generalization. The selected H1 can improve the system's finite retained output without establishing that its historical rationale was correct.",
