    {
      "id": "v1/5nn4_SC2_A_1017__top1/r03/G4",
      "evidence_sha256": "3009950e3fb73119630aac8cb44fb1ed7242acb59d1ef3015ab29e5729c8f4e9",
      "assessment": "R3 G4 correctly orients incumbent-minus-latest +0.050904 and acknowledges all quartile means are negative in the treatment direction. H1 [7,5,6,5] extends early guidance; H2 [6,5,5,5] removes the third-window increment. Yet it imports the unsupported 0.03 threshold, calls Q4's large loss noise without tracing the candidate, and says all quartiles favor latest in memory despite the opposite numbers. Selected H1 gives R4 Mean 4.190014.",
      "decision_update": "Reconcile public memory with the actual signed quartile table before publication. Keep Mean primary while reporting influential candidates and paired medians as sensitivity information, rather than replacing the objective with a mandatory median gain. The early extension is a test of a local response, not a generic rule that the largest-displacement interval must be best.",
      "counterexample_or_limitation": "H1 improves the fixed-group mean relative to its source, but restart parents changed and the gain is concentrated; that does not validate the noise threshold or the inferred mechanism. The discarded H2 remains a proposal with no R4 outcome.",
